---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PHONES, RESULTS, LEGEND, SHIELD, backView, sectionView } from '../lib/shield';
---

<Base
  title="suñůlink.shield, to scale"
  description="suñůlink.shield drawn to scale from the parametric CAD: battery, thickness, weight and a section through the magnet centre, on iPhone 18 Pro and on a phone with a camera island."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">suñůlink.shield · to scale</p>
      <h1>One shield.<br />Drawn to scale.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A mesh node on the back of the phone: HaLow radio for the neighbourhood mesh, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth to the phone, its
        own 14 Wh battery, charged over USB-C from a wall charger or power bank. Every drawing here is to scale and
        comes from the same parametric CAD that exports STEP and STL for CNC and tooling.
      </p>
      <p class="fits">
        Fits every iPhone back to iPhone X, and Google Pixel and Samsung Galaxy phones, flagship and everyday, with a case
        made for each model. Drawn here on the two reference shapes: iPhone 18 Pro’s full-width camera plateau, and a camera
        island like most other phones.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section explorer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <form class="pick" aria-label="Choose a phone and whether to show the internals">
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Phone</legend>
          {PHONES.map((p, i) => (
            <label><input type="radio" name="phone" value={p.id} checked={i === 0} /> <span>{p.short}</span></label>
          ))}
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>View</legend>
          <label><input type="checkbox" name="internals" checked /> <span>Show internals</span></label>
        </fieldset>
      </form>

      <div class="views">
        {PHONES.map((p) => {
          const r = RESULTS[p.id][SHIELD];
          return (
            <article class="view" data-phone={p.id}>
              <div class="draw">
                <div class="back" set:html={backView(p, SHIELD, 2.4, true)} />
              </div>
              <div class="info">
                <h2>suñůlink.shield <small>on the {p.short}</small></h2>
                <p class="line">
                  {p.id === 'iphone-18-pro'
                    ? 'The back below the camera plateau, 3 mm above the lens tops, its top edge angled so no camera ever sees it.'
                    : 'The whole back around the camera island, 3 mm above the lens tops, the camera in a well angled clear of every field of view.'}
                </p>
                <dl class="stats">
                  <div><dt>{r.wh} Wh</dt><dd>battery, {r.cm3} cm³ of cells</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>{r.t} mm</dt><dd>thick, {r.proud} mm above the lens tops</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>{r.tiG} g</dt><dd>in titanium</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>about {r.wh.toFixed(0)} h</dt><dd>relaying on its own cells (estimate)</dd></div>
                </dl>
                <p class="small">
                  Footprint {r.footprint[0]} × {r.footprint[1]} mm. Magnet ring {r.ring} mm. Charges over its USB-C from a wall
                  charger or power bank. When its cells run out it takes a little from the phone through its Qi2 coil, where the
                  phone supports it, or over a short USB-C cable.
                </p>
                <h3>Section through the magnet centre</h3>
                <div class="section-draw" set:html={sectionView(p, SHIELD)} />
                <ul class="legend" role="list">
                  {LEGEND.map((l) => (
                    <li><i class:list={[{ dashed: l.dashed }]} style={`--c:${l.color}`} />{l.label}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </article>
          );
        })}
      </div>

      <p class="small note">
        From the CAD. Cells at 0.45 Wh/cm³ (thin pouch). Relay time assumes about 1 W for the board and radios, an estimate
        until the board exists. The build fails if the shield covers a lens, the flash, the depth sensor or the microphone, or
        clips a field of view. iPhone 18 Pro dimensions are measured from Apple’s published model; the makers’ accessory
        drawings take precedence when available.
      </p>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/buy">Reserve one</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://dev.khensu.nu/shell">Full specifications</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/#shell-title">Back to the overview</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede,
  .fits {
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .fits {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }
  .pick {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
  }
  fieldset {
    border: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  legend {
    float: left;
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  label {
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  label input {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  label span {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  label input:checked + span {
    background: rgba(139, 123, 255, 0.18);
    border-color: #8b7bff;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  label input:focus-visible + span {
    outline: 2px solid #8b7bff;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .view {
    display: none;
  }
  .view {
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 1.4rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035);
  }
  .explorer:has(input[name='phone'][value='iphone-18-pro']:checked) .view[data-phone='iphone-18-pro'],
  .explorer:has(input[name='phone'][value='island']:checked) .view[data-phone='island'] {
    display: grid;
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .explorer:has(input[name='internals']:not(:checked)) :global(.internals) {
    display: none;
  }

  .draw {
    padding: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #0b0b0e;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }
  .draw :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .info h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .info h2 small {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .line {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 2.2rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .stats dt {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #b9b0ff;
  }
  .stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .section-draw {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .section-draw :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .legend {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .legend li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }
  .legend i {
    width: 20px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--c);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .legend i.dashed {
    height: 0;
    background: none;
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--c);
  }

  .btn-row {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .view {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .draw {
      justify-self: center;
      max-width: 240px;
    }
  }
</style>
